TWO FURTHER CAVEATS WORTH KNOWING
  - License: INSTALL.md says the model is under the Qwen Research License - research/evaluation only,
    commercial use forbidden. That is a materially different position from the currently deployed
    FLUX.1-schnell int4, which is Apache-2.0, and it matters given the user's earlier note about possibly
    publishing and partially commercialising work.
  - Content: the GGUF is the "Uncensored" variant. The author's own note: "该 GGUF 属 Uncensored 系，
    介意可装完后自行替换".

BETTER PATH FOUND - OPENVINO ALREADY KNOWS QWEN-IMAGE
  Checked the installed runtime instead of assuming:
      openvino_genai 2026.4.1.0
      classes: QwenImageTransformer2DModel, Qwen3TextEncoder   <- both present
      Text2ImagePipeline factories: flux, latent_consistency_model, stable_diffusion,
                                    stable_diffusion_3, stable_diffusion_xl
  So the underlying architecture IS supported, but there is still no high-level `qwen_image` factory -
  the same situation FLUX and Z-Image were in before their factories landed. Once upstream adds
  `qwen_image`, switching would be a one-line environment change on the iGPU (no ComfyUI, no XPU torch,
  no uncensored weights), exactly like the LCM -> FLUX migration.

RECOMMENDATION
  Do not install route A on this machine: the author's own detection rejects the GPU, the real download is
  ~2.3x what the plan stated, two mandatory prerequisites were omitted, and the weights are research-only.
  Keep FLUX int4 (8.61 GB, iGPU, 13-18 s/image, Apache-2.0) as the local generation path.
  Revisit Qwen-Image when openvino_genai exposes a qwen_image factory; the plugin source is already
  downloaded and kept in case a discrete-GPU machine becomes available.

